  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Ram Niwas vs State Of Haryana on 21 April, 2016 Author: T.P.S. Mann Bench: T.P.S. Mann In The High Court Of Punjab And Haryana At Chandigarh Crl. Revision 1391 of 2009 Date of Decision : April 22, 2016 Ram Niwas .....Petitioner Versus State of Haryana .....Respondent Coram: Hon'Ble Mr. Justice T.P.S. Mann Present : Mr. Gurinder Pal Singh, Advocate Mr. Dhruv Dayal, Deputy A.G., Haryana T.P.S. Mann, J. (Oral)",
    "facts": "Aggrieved of his conviction and sentence, the petitioner filed an appeal. 1 of 2 Still not satisfied, he filed the present revision which was admitted on 25.5.2009. Subsequently vide order dated 8.6.2009, this Court was pleased to grant him bail. On the last date of hearing, learned counsel for the petitioner apprised the Court that the petitioner had already passed away. Learned State counsel, accordingly, prayed for a short adjournment for obtaining verification of the said fact. Learned State counsel has produced the affidavit executed by Ajeet Singh, Assistance Commissioner of Police, Manesar wherein it stands mentioned that the petitioner had expired on 17.10.2011 while in Artimis Hospital, Gurgaon.",
